LED."],"color":"#232","bgcolor":"#353"},{"id":107,"type":"Note","pos":[-1473.3956604433931,-232.05675550811694],"size":[518.5082585211327,519.4710939070534],"flags":{},"order":5,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["Note: this version of the workflow uses the following in case you have VAE issues:\nhttps://github.com/stduhpf/ComfyUI--WanImageToVideoTiled\n\nNew Minimal Universal Workflow for Wan2.2 5b in ComfyUI.\n5billion parameters with minimal VRAM usage, for image to video.\ntry setting Ksampler steps from 2 to 4, with dpmpp_2m_heun (not GPU version)\nOr ModelSamplingSD3 from to 5 to 20, or bypass ModelSampling for varying results.\n\nMain model file, Wan 5b GGUF:\nhttps://huggingface.co/hum-ma/Wan2.2-TI2V-5B-Turbo-GGUF/tree/main\nWan2_2-TI2V-5B-Turbo-Q5_K_S.gguf\n\nLightweight VAEs are now officially supported in ComfyUI.\nhttps://huggingface.co/lightx2v/Autoencoders/tree/main\nlighttaew2_2.safetensors\n\nfull VAE currently needed for encoding and other functions:\nhttps://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Wan_2.2_ComfyUI_Repackaged/tree/main/split_files/vae\nwan2.2_vae.safetensors\n\nGGUF loader node from github user 'city96', Text Encoder:\nhttps://huggingface.co/city96/umt5-xxl-encoder-gguf/tree/main\numt5-xxl-encoder-Q3_K_S.gguf\n(Note, there are nodes out there for caching prompts for 2x speed)\nI also have custom code for this if CFZ nodes doesn't work for you.\n\nPut model files in correct folders.\nwan2.2_vae goes into the /ComfyUI/models/vae\nlighttaew2_2 goes in /ComfyUI/models/vae_approx\n\nFor CFG guidance above 1.0, connect Negative prompt to Ksampler.\nFor sparse distilled models like Wan Turbo stay at 1.0 CFG, but you can try maybe 1.2 or similarly low settings with others. (time per step will essentially double)\n\nDark purple nodes are simply disabled. Right-click then choose 'bypass' to reactivate them for testing.  Not all samplers are supported, recommended: dpmpp_2m_heun, dpmpp_3m, gradient estimation, res multi, or uniPC, all with simple or sgm_uniform scheduler.\n\nMachine learning workloads cause excess heat, watch temps, adjust accordingly."],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"}],"links":[[180,60,0,6,0,"CLIP"],[182,60,0,7,0,"CLIP"],[314,65,0,92,0,"MODEL"],[336,103,0,105,1,"VAE"],[337,92,0,105,0,"LATENT"],[339,106,0,61,0,"MODEL"],[348,61,0,111,0,"MODEL"],[349,111,0,65,0,"MODEL"],[380,105,0,118,0,"IMAGE"],[383,108,0,120,0,"VAE"],[385,120,0,92,3,"LATENT"],[386,114,0,120,1,"IMAGE"],[387,6,0,92,1,"CONDITIONING"],[388,6,0,92,2,"CONDITIONING"]],"groups":[],"config":{},"extra":{"ds":{"scale":0.8954302432553067,"offset":[1631.8778484042614,489.4603781793527]},"frontendVersion":"1.34.9","workflowRendererVersion":"LG"},"version":0.4}